# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Orbit — Payments (Razorpay) credentials
#
# Copy the vars you need into your main .env to switch Orbit from MANUAL mode
# (payments recorded directly, plan upgrades applied immediately, a mock order
# id standing in for Razorpay) to LIVE online collection via Razorpay.
#
# Behaviour:
#   • Both RAZORPAY_KEY_ID + RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET set → live Razorpay order
#     creation (falls back to a mock order on any error).
#   • Either missing → manual mode (dev/demo safe).
#
# See lib/payments.ts (PAYMENTS_SETUP_DOC) for the full walkthrough.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public key id — rzp_test_* for sandbox, rzp_live_* for production.
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Key secret — server-only. NEVER expose this to the browser.
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=your-razorpay-key-secret

# Required for app/api/webhooks/razorpay to do anything. HMAC-SHA256 secret
# used to verify Razorpay webhook signatures before recording a payment,
# marking an invoice Paid, or activating a paid plan. Without it the webhook
# route returns 503 and orders are never settled automatically — set it on
# your webhook in the Razorpay dashboard (Settings → Webhooks → subscribe to
# "payment.captured") and mirror it here.
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your-webhook-signing-secret

# ── Where to get keys ──
# 1. Sign up at https://dashboard.razorpay.com and switch to Test Mode.
# 2. Settings → API Keys → Generate Test Key → copy Key Id + Key Secret.
# 3. (Webhooks) Settings → Webhooks → add your endpoint + signing secret.
#
# Production note: creating an order is only step 1. After the customer pays,
# verify the Razorpay webhook signature (HMAC-SHA256 over the raw body with
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET) — or the checkout callback signature — BEFORE calling
# recordPayment() and marking the invoice Paid.
